        -:20732:**     assert( X || CORRUPT_DB );
        -:20733:**
        -:20734:** CORRUPT_DB is true during normal operation.  CORRUPT_DB does not indicate
        -:20735:** that the database is definitely corrupt, only that it might be corrupt.
        -:20736:** For most test cases, CORRUPT_DB is set to false using a special
        -:20737:** sqlite3_test_control().  This enables assert() statements to prove
        -:20738:** things that are always true for well-formed databases.
        -:20739:*/
        -:20740:#define CORRUPT_DB  (sqlite3Config.neverCorrupt==0)
