        -:22172:**
        -:22173:** sqlite3MemdebugHasType() returns true if any of the bits in its second
        -:22174:** argument match the type set by the previous sqlite3MemdebugSetType().
        -:22175:** sqlite3MemdebugHasType() is intended for use inside assert() statements.
        -:22176:**
        -:22177:** sqlite3MemdebugNoType() returns true if none of the bits in its second
        -:22178:** argument match the type set by the previous sqlite3MemdebugSetType().
        -:22179:**
        -:22180:** Perhaps the most important point is the difference between MEMTYPE_HEAP
        -:22181:** and MEMTYPE_LOOKASIDE.  If an allocation is MEMTYPE_LOOKASIDE, that means
        -:22182:** it might have been allocated by lookaside, except the allocation was
        -:22183:** too large or lookaside was already full.  It is important to verify
        -:22184:** that allocations that might have been satisfied by lookaside are not
        -:22185:** passed back to non-lookaside free() routines.  Asserts such as the
        -:22186:** example above are placed on the non-lookaside free() routines to verify
        -:22187:** this constraint.
        -:22188:**
