        -:23351:
        -:23352:/* Statement journals spill to disk when their size exceeds the following
        -:23353:** threshold (in bytes). 0 means that statement journals are created and
        -:23354:** written to disk immediately (the default behavior for SQLite versions
        -:23355:** before 3.12.0).  -1 means always keep the entire statement journal in
        -:23356:** memory.  (The statement journal is also always held entirely in memory
        -:23357:** if journal_mode=MEMORY or if temp_store=MEMORY, regardless of this
        -:23358:** setting.)
