        -:23490:/*
        -:23491:** The value of the "pending" byte must be 0x40000000 (1 byte past the
        -:23492:** 1-gibabyte boundary) in a compatible database.  SQLite never uses
        -:23493:** the database page that contains the pending byte.  It never attempts
        -:23494:** to read or write that page.  The pending byte page is set aside
        -:23495:** for use by the VFS layers as space for managing file locks.
        -:23496:**
        -:23497:** During testing, it is often desirable to move the pending byte to
        -:23498:** a different position in the file.  This allows code that has to
        -:23499:** deal with the pending byte to run on files that are much smaller
        -:23500:** than 1 GiB.  The sqlite3_test_control() interface can be used to
        -:23501:** move the pending byte.
        -:23502:**
        -:23503:** IMPORTANT:  Changing the pending byte to any value other than
        -:23504:** 0x40000000 results in an incompatible database file format!
        -:23505:** Changing the pending byte during operation will result in undefined
        -:23506:** and incorrect behavior.
        -:23507:*/
        -:23508:#ifndef SQLITE_OMIT_WSD
        -:23509:SQLITE_PRIVATE int sqlite3PendingByte = 0x40000000;
        -:23510:#endif
