        -:38854:******************************************************************************
        -:38855:**
        -:38856:** This file contains the VFS implementation for unix-like operating systems
        -:38857:** include Linux, MacOSX, *BSD, QNX, VxWorks, AIX, HPUX, and others.
        -:38858:**
        -:38859:** There are actually several different VFS implementations in this file.
        -:38860:** The differences are in the way that file locking is done.  The default
        -:38861:** implementation uses Posix Advisory Locks.  Alternative implementations
        -:38862:** use flock(), dot-files, various proprietary locking schemas, or simply
        -:38863:** skip locking all together.
        -:38864:**
        -:38865:** This source file is organized into divisions where the logic for various
        -:38866:** subfunctions is contained within the appropriate division.  PLEASE
        -:38867:** KEEP THE STRUCTURE OF THIS FILE INTACT.  New code should be placed
        -:38868:** in the correct division and should be clearly labelled.
        -:38869:**
        -:38870:** The layout of divisions is as follows:
        -:38871:**
        -:38872:**   *  General-purpose declarations and utility functions.
        -:38873:**   *  Unique file ID logic used by VxWorks.
        -:38874:**   *  Various locking primitive implementations (all except proxy locking):
        -:38875:**      + for Posix Advisory Locks
        -:38876:**      + for no-op locks
        -:38877:**      + for dot-file locks
        -:38878:**      + for flock() locking
        -:38879:**      + for named semaphore locks (VxWorks only)
        -:38880:**      + for AFP filesystem locks (MacOSX only)
        -:38881:**   *  sqlite3_file methods not associated with locking.
        -:38882:**   *  Definitions of sqlite3_io_methods objects for all locking
        -:38883:**      methods plus "finder" functions for each locking method.
        -:38884:**   *  sqlite3_vfs method implementations.
        -:38885:**   *  Locking primitives for the proxy uber-locking-method. (MacOSX only)
        -:38886:**   *  Definitions of sqlite3_vfs objects for all locking methods
        -:38887:**      plus implementations of sqlite3_os_init() and sqlite3_os_end().
        -:38888:*/
