        -:44365:**
        -:44366:**
        -:44367:** A pointer to the F pointer is used as the pAppData value for VFS
        -:44368:** objects.  We have to do this instead of letting pAppData point
        -:44369:** directly at the finder-function since C90 rules prevent a void*
        -:44370:** from be cast into a function pointer.
