        -:53848:/* Storage for a memdb file.
        -:53849:**
        -:53850:** An memdb object can be shared or separate.  Shared memdb objects can be
        -:53851:** used by more than one database connection.  Mutexes are used by shared
        -:53852:** memdb objects to coordinate access.  Separate memdb objects are only
        -:53853:** connected to a single database connection and do not require additional
        -:53854:** mutexes.
        -:53855:**
        -:53856:** Shared memdb objects have .zFName!=0 and .pMutex!=0.  They are created
        -:53857:** using "file:/name?vfs=memdb".  The first character of the name must be
        -:53858:** "/" or else the object will be a separate memdb object.  All shared
        -:53859:** memdb objects are stored in memdb_g.apMemStore[] in an arbitrary order.
        -:53860:**
        -:53861:** Separate memdb objects are created using a name that does not begin
        -:53862:** with "/" or using sqlite3_deserialize().
        -:53863:**
        -:53864:** Access rules for shared MemStore objects:
