        -:58417:/*
        -:58418:** The Pager.eLock variable is almost always set to one of the
        -:58419:** following locking-states, according to the lock currently held on
        -:58420:** the database file: NO_LOCK, SHARED_LOCK, RESERVED_LOCK or EXCLUSIVE_LOCK.
        -:58421:** This variable is kept up to date as locks are taken and released by
        -:58422:** the pagerLockDb() and pagerUnlockDb() wrappers.
        -:58423:**
        -:58424:** If the VFS xLock() or xUnlock() returns an error other than SQLITE_BUSY
        -:58425:** (i.e. one of the SQLITE_IOERR subtypes), it is not clear whether or not
        -:58426:** the operation was successful. In these circumstances pagerLockDb() and
        -:58427:** pagerUnlockDb() take a conservative approach - eLock is always updated
        -:58428:** when unlocking the file, and only updated when locking the file if the
        -:58429:** VFS call is successful. This way, the Pager.eLock variable may be set
        -:58430:** to a less exclusive (lower) value than the lock that is actually held
        -:58431:** at the system level, but it is never set to a more exclusive value.
        -:58432:**
        -:58433:** This is usually safe. If an xUnlock fails or appears to fail, there may
        -:58434:** be a few redundant xLock() calls or a lock may be held for longer than
        -:58435:** required, but nothing really goes wrong.
        -:58436:**
        -:58437:** The exception is when the database file is unlocked as the pager moves
        -:58438:** from ERROR to OPEN state. At this point there may be a hot-journal file
        -:58439:** in the file-system that needs to be rolled back (as part of an OPEN->SHARED
        -:58440:** transition, by the same pager or any other). If the call to xUnlock()
        -:58441:** fails at this point and the pager is left holding an EXCLUSIVE lock, this
        -:58442:** can confuse the call to xCheckReservedLock() call made later as part
        -:58443:** of hot-journal detection.
        -:58444:**
