        -:58446:** lock held by this process or any others". So xCheckReservedLock may
        -:58447:** return true because the caller itself is holding an EXCLUSIVE lock (but
        -:58448:** doesn't know it because of a previous error in xUnlock). If this happens
        -:58449:** a hot-journal may be mistaken for a journal being created by an active
        -:58450:** transaction in another process, causing SQLite to read from the database
        -:58451:** without rolling it back.
        -:58452:**
        -:58453:** To work around this, if a call to xUnlock() fails when unlocking the
        -:58454:** database in the ERROR state, Pager.eLock is set to UNKNOWN_LOCK. It
        -:58455:** is only changed back to a real locking state after a successful call
        -:58456:** to xLock(EXCLUSIVE). Also, the code to do the OPEN->SHARED state transition
        -:58457:** omits the check for a hot-journal if Pager.eLock is set to UNKNOWN_LOCK
        -:58458:** lock. Instead, it assumes a hot-journal exists and obtains an EXCLUSIVE
        -:58459:** lock on the database file before attempting to roll it back. See function
        -:58460:** PagerSharedLock() for more detail.
        -:58461:**
        -:58462:** Pager.eLock may only be set to UNKNOWN_LOCK when the pager is in
        -:58463:** PAGER_OPEN state.
        -:58464:*/
        -:58465:#define UNKNOWN_LOCK                (EXCLUSIVE_LOCK+1)
