        -:58661:**   is set to zero in all other states. In PAGER_ERROR state, Pager.errCode
        -:58662:**   is always set to SQLITE_FULL, SQLITE_IOERR or one of the SQLITE_IOERR_XXX
        -:58663:**   sub-codes.
        -:58664:**
        -:58665:** syncFlags, walSyncFlags
        -:58666:**
        -:58667:**   syncFlags is either SQLITE_SYNC_NORMAL (0x02) or SQLITE_SYNC_FULL (0x03).
        -:58668:**   syncFlags is used for rollback mode.  walSyncFlags is used for WAL mode
        -:58669:**   and contains the flags used to sync the checkpoint operations in the
        -:58670:**   lower two bits, and sync flags used for transaction commits in the WAL
        -:58671:**   file in bits 0x04 and 0x08.  In other words, to get the correct sync flags
        -:58672:**   for checkpoint operations, use (walSyncFlags&0x03) and to get the correct
        -:58673:**   sync flags for transaction commit, use ((walSyncFlags>>2)&0x03).  Note
