        -:63520:** The page getter methods each try to acquire a reference to a
        -:63521:** page with page number pgno. If the requested reference is
        -:63522:** successfully obtained, it is copied to *ppPage and SQLITE_OK returned.
        -:63523:**
        -:63524:** There are different implementations of the getter method depending
        -:63525:** on the current state of the pager.
        -:63526:**
        -:63527:**     getPageNormal()         --  The normal getter
        -:63528:**     getPageError()          --  Used if the pager is in an error state
        -:63529:**     getPageMmap()           --  Used if memory-mapped I/O is enabled
        -:63530:**
        -:63531:** If the requested page is already in the cache, it is returned.
        -:63532:** Otherwise, a new page object is allocated and populated with data
        -:63533:** read from the database file. In some cases, the pcache module may
        -:63534:** choose not to allocate a new page object and may reuse an existing
        -:63535:** object with no outstanding references.
        -:63536:**
        -:63537:** The extra data appended to a page is always initialized to zeros the
        -:63538:** first time a page is loaded into memory. If the page requested is
        -:63539:** already in the cache when this function is called, then the extra
        -:63540:** data is left as it was when the page object was last used.
        -:63541:**
        -:63542:** If the database image is smaller than the requested page or if
        -:63543:** the flags parameter contains the PAGER_GET_NOCONTENT bit and the
        -:63544:** requested page is not already stored in the cache, then no
        -:63545:** actual disk read occurs. In this case the memory image of the
        -:63546:** page is initialized to all zeros.
        -:63547:**
        -:63548:** If PAGER_GET_NOCONTENT is true, it means that we do not care about
        -:63549:** the contents of the page. This occurs in two scenarios:
        -:63550:**
        -:63551:**   a) When reading a free-list leaf page from the database, and
        -:63552:**
        -:63553:**   b) When a savepoint is being rolled back and we need to load
        -:63554:**      a new page into the cache to be filled with the data read
        -:63555:**      from the savepoint journal.
        -:63556:**
        -:63557:** If PAGER_GET_NOCONTENT is true, then the data returned is zeroed instead
        -:63558:** of being read from the database. Additionally, the bits corresponding
