        -:66158:/*
        -:66159:** Index numbers for various locking bytes.   WAL_NREADER is the number
        -:66160:** of available reader locks and should be at least 3.  The default
        -:66161:** is SQLITE_SHM_NLOCK==8 and  WAL_NREADER==5.
        -:66162:**
        -:66163:** Technically, the various VFSes are free to implement these locks however
        -:66164:** they see fit.  However, compatibility is encouraged so that VFSes can
        -:66165:** interoperate.  The standard implementation used on both unix and windows
        -:66166:** is for the index number to indicate a byte offset into the
        -:66167:** WalCkptInfo.aLock[] array in the wal-index header.  In other words, all
        -:66168:** locks are on the shm file.  The WALINDEX_LOCK_OFFSET constant (which
        -:66169:** should be 120) is the location in the shm file for the first locking
        -:66170:** byte.
