        -:72184:**   2) When a free-list leaf page is reused, its content is not read
        -:72185:**      from the database or written to the journal file (why should it
        -:72186:**      be, if it is not at all meaningful?).
        -:72187:**
        -:72188:** By themselves, these optimizations work fine and provide a handy
        -:72189:** performance boost to bulk delete or insert operations. However, if
        -:72190:** a page is moved to the free-list and then reused within the same
        -:72191:** transaction, a problem comes up. If the page is not journalled when
        -:72192:** it is moved to the free-list and it is also not journalled when it
        -:72193:** is extracted from the free-list and reused, then the original data
        -:72194:** may be lost. In the event of a rollback, it may not be possible
