        -:95324:/*****************************************************************************
        -:95325:** What follows is a massive switch statement where each case implements a
        -:95326:** separate instruction in the virtual machine.  If we follow the usual
        -:95327:** indentation conventions, each case should be indented by 6 spaces.  But
        -:95328:** that is a lot of wasted space on the left margin.  So the code within
        -:95329:** the switch statement will break with convention and be flush-left. Another
        -:95330:** big comment (similar to this one) will mark the point in the code where
        -:95331:** we transition back to normal indentation.
        -:95332:**
        -:95333:** The formatting of each case is important.  The makefile for SQLite
        -:95334:** generates two C files "opcodes.h" and "opcodes.c" by scanning this
        -:95335:** file looking for lines that begin with "case OP_".  The opcodes.h files
        -:95336:** will be filled with #defines that give unique integer values to each
        -:95337:** opcode and the opcodes.c file is filled with an array of strings where
        -:95338:** each string is the symbolic name for the corresponding opcode.  If the
        -:95339:** case statement is followed by a comment of the form "/# same as ... #/"
        -:95340:** that comment is used to determine the particular value of the opcode.
        -:95341:**
        -:95342:** Other keywords in the comment that follows each case are used to
        -:95343:** construct the OPFLG_INITIALIZER value that initializes opcodeProperty[].
        -:95344:** Keywords include: in1, in2, in3, out2, out3.  See
        -:95345:** the mkopcodeh.awk script for additional information.
        -:95346:**
        -:95347:** Documentation about VDBE opcodes is generated by scanning this file
        -:95348:** for lines of that contain "Opcode:".  That line and all subsequent
        -:95349:** comment lines are used in the generation of the opcode.html documentation
        -:95350:** file.
        -:95351:**
        -:95352:** SUMMARY:
        -:95353:**
