        -:104343:** 5 key to the current key of PmaReader 4 (still "Grapefruit"). The PmaReader
        -:104344:** 5 value is still smaller, so aTree[6] is set to 5. And so on up the tree.
        -:104345:** The value of PmaReader 6 - "Durian" - is now smaller than that of PmaReader
        -:104346:** 5, so aTree[3] is set to 6. Key 0 is smaller than key 6 (Banana<Durian),
        -:104347:** so the value written into element 1 of the array is 0. As follows:
        -:104348:**
        -:104349:**     aTree[] = { X, 0   0, 6    0, 3, 5, 6 }
        -:104350:**
        -:104351:** In other words, each time we advance to the next sorter element, log2(N)
        -:104352:** key comparison operations are required, where N is the number of segments
        -:104353:** being merged (rounded up to the next power of 2).
