        -:110131:**
        -:110132:** To resolve table columns references we look for nodes (or subtrees) of the
        -:110133:** form X.Y.Z or Y.Z or just Z where
        -:110134:**
        -:110135:**      X:   The name of a database.  Ex:  "main" or "temp" or
        -:110136:**           the symbolic name assigned to an ATTACH-ed database.
        -:110137:**
        -:110138:**      Y:   The name of a table in a FROM clause.  Or in a trigger
        -:110139:**           one of the special names "old" or "new".
        -:110140:**
        -:110141:**      Z:   The name of a column in table Y.
        -:110142:**
        -:110143:** The node at the root of the subtree is modified as follows:
        -:110144:**
        -:110145:**    Expr.op        Changed to TK_COLUMN
        -:110146:**    Expr.pTab      Points to the Table object for X.Y
        -:110147:**    Expr.iColumn   The column index in X.Y.  -1 for the rowid.
