        -:148266:/*
        -:148267:** Alternative compound select code generator for cases when there
        -:148268:** is an ORDER BY clause.
        -:148269:**
        -:148270:** We assume a query of the following form:
        -:148271:**
        -:148272:**      <selectA>  <operator>  <selectB>  ORDER BY <orderbylist>
        -:148273:**
        -:148274:** <operator> is one of UNION ALL, UNION, EXCEPT, or INTERSECT.  The idea
        -:148275:** is to code both <selectA> and <selectB> with the ORDER BY clause as
        -:148276:** co-routines.  Then run the co-routines in parallel and merge the results
        -:148277:** into the output.  In addition to the two coroutines (called selectA and
        -:148278:** selectB) there are 7 subroutines:
        -:148279:**
        -:148280:**    outA:    Move the output of the selectA coroutine into the output
        -:148281:**             of the compound query.
        -:148282:**
        -:148283:**    outB:    Move the output of the selectB coroutine into the output
        -:148284:**             of the compound query.  (Only generated for UNION and
        -:148285:**             UNION ALL.  EXCEPT and INSERTSECT never output a row that
        -:148286:**             appears only in B.)
        -:148287:**
        -:148288:**    AltB:    Called when there is data from both coroutines and A<B.
        -:148289:**
        -:148290:**    AeqB:    Called when there is data from both coroutines and A==B.
        -:148291:**
        -:148292:**    AgtB:    Called when there is data from both coroutines and A>B.
        -:148293:**
