        -:148299:** <operator> is used:
        -:148300:**
        -:148301:**
        -:148302:**             UNION ALL         UNION            EXCEPT          INTERSECT
        -:148303:**          -------------  -----------------  --------------  -----------------
        -:148304:**   AltB:   outA, nextA      outA, nextA       outA, nextA         nextA
        -:148305:**
        -:148306:**   AeqB:   outA, nextA         nextA             nextA         outA, nextA
        -:148307:**
        -:148308:**   AgtB:   outB, nextB      outB, nextB          nextB            nextB
        -:148309:**
        -:148310:**   EofA:   outB, nextB      outB, nextB          halt             halt
        -:148311:**
        -:148312:**   EofB:   outA, nextA      outA, nextA       outA, nextA         halt
        -:148313:**
        -:148314:** In the AltB, AeqB, and AgtB subroutines, an EOF on A following nextA
        -:148315:** causes an immediate jump to EofA and an EOF on B following nextB causes
        -:148316:** an immediate jump to EofB.  Within EofA and EofB, and EOF on entry or
        -:148317:** following nextX causes a jump to the end of the select processing.
        -:148318:**
        -:148319:** Duplicate removal in the UNION, EXCEPT, and INTERSECT cases is handled
        -:148320:** within the output subroutine.  The regPrev register set holds the previously
        -:148321:** output value.  A comparison is made against this value and the output
        -:148322:** is skipped if the next results would be the same as the previous.
        -:148323:**
        -:148324:** The implementation plan is to implement the two coroutines and seven
        -:148325:** subroutines first, then put the control logic at the bottom.  Like this:
        -:148326:**
        -:148327:**          goto Init
        -:148328:**     coA: coroutine for left query (A)
        -:148329:**     coB: coroutine for right query (B)
        -:148330:**    outA: output one row of A
        -:148331:**    outB: output one row of B (UNION and UNION ALL only)
        -:148332:**    EofA: ...
        -:148333:**    EofB: ...
        -:148334:**    AltB: ...
        -:148335:**    AeqB: ...
        -:148336:**    AgtB: ...
        -:148337:**    Init: initialize coroutine registers
        -:148338:**          yield coA
        -:148339:**          if eof(A) goto EofA
        -:148340:**          yield coB
        -:148341:**          if eof(B) goto EofB
        -:148342:**    Cmpr: Compare A, B
        -:148343:**          Jump AltB, AeqB, AgtB
        -:148344:**     End: ...
        -:148345:**
        -:148346:** We call AltB, AeqB, AgtB, EofA, and EofB "subroutines" but they are not
        -:148347:** actually called using Gosub and they do not Return.  EofA and EofB loop
        -:148348:** until all data is exhausted then jump to the "end" label.  AltB, AeqB,
        -:148349:** and AgtB jump to either L2 or to one of EofA or EofB.
