        -:157207:/*
        -:157208:** The VACUUM command is used to clean up the database,
        -:157209:** collapse free space, etc.  It is modelled after the VACUUM command
        -:157210:** in PostgreSQL.  The VACUUM command works as follows:
        -:157211:**
        -:157212:**   (1)  Create a new transient database file
        -:157213:**   (2)  Copy all content from the database being vacuumed into
        -:157214:**        the new transient database file
        -:157215:**   (3)  Copy content from the transient database back into the
        -:157216:**        original database.
        -:157217:**
        -:157218:** The transient database requires temporary disk space approximately
        -:157219:** equal to the size of the original database.  The copy operation of
        -:157220:** step (3) requires additional temporary disk space approximately equal
        -:157221:** to the size of the original database for the rollback journal.
        -:157222:** Hence, temporary disk space that is approximately 2x the size of the
        -:157223:** original database is required.  Every page of the database is written
        -:157224:** approximately 3 times:  Once for step (2) and twice for step (3).
        -:157225:** Two writes per page are required in step (3) because the original
        -:157226:** database content must be written into the rollback journal prior to
        -:157227:** overwriting the database with the vacuumed content.
        -:157228:**
        -:157229:** Only 1x temporary space and only 1x writes would be required if
        -:157230:** the copy of step (3) were replaced by deleting the original database
        -:157231:** and renaming the transient database as the original.  But that will
        -:157232:** not work if other processes are attached to the original database.
        -:157233:** And a power loss in between deleting the original and renaming the
        -:157234:** transient would cause the database file to appear to be deleted
        -:157235:** following reboot.
        -:157236:*/
