        -:159069:/*
        -:159070:** Each instance of this object represents an algorithm for evaluating one
        -:159071:** term of a join.  Every term of the FROM clause will have at least
        -:159072:** one corresponding WhereLoop object (unless INDEXED BY constraints
        -:159073:** prevent a query solution - which is an error) and many terms of the
        -:159074:** FROM clause will have multiple WhereLoop objects, each describing a
        -:159075:** potential way of implementing that FROM-clause term, together with
        -:159076:** dependencies and cost estimates for using the chosen algorithm.
        -:159077:**
        -:159078:** Query planning consists of building up a collection of these WhereLoop
        -:159079:** objects, then computing a particular sequence of WhereLoop objects, with
        -:159080:** one WhereLoop object per FROM clause term, that satisfy all dependencies
        -:159081:** and that minimize the overall cost.
