        -:160151:** the vector contains only index terms and those terms are in the correct
        -:160152:** order.  The modified IN expression is returned.  The caller is responsible
        -:160153:** for deleting the returned expression.
        -:160154:**
        -:160155:** Example:
        -:160156:**
        -:160157:**    CREATE TABLE t1(a,b,c,d,e,f);
        -:160158:**    CREATE INDEX t1x1 ON t1(e,c);
        -:160159:**    SELECT * FROM t1 WHERE (a,b,c,d,e) IN (SELECT v,w,x,y,z FROM t2)
        -:160160:**                           \_______________________________________/
        -:160161:**                                     The pX expression
        -:160162:**
        -:160163:** Since only columns e and c can be used with the index, in that order,
        -:160164:** the modified IN expression that is returned will be:
        -:160165:**
        -:160166:**        (e,c) IN (SELECT z,x FROM t2)
