        -:173710:**   in an array of accumulator registers - one for each window function
        -:173711:**   in the WindowCodeArg.pMWin list.
        -:173712:**
        -:173713:** eDelete:
        -:173714:**   The window functions implementation sometimes caches the input rows
        -:173715:**   that it processes in a temporary table. If it is not zero, this
        -:173716:**   variable indicates when rows may be removed from the temp table (in
        -:173717:**   order to reduce memory requirements - it would always be safe just
        -:173718:**   to leave them there). Possible values for eDelete are:
        -:173719:**
        -:173720:**      WINDOW_RETURN_ROW:
        -:173721:**        An input row can be discarded after it is returned to the caller.
        -:173722:**
        -:173723:**      WINDOW_AGGINVERSE:
