        -:175709:/* The next sections is a series of control #defines.
        -:175710:** various aspects of the generated parser.
        -:175711:**    YYCODETYPE         is the data type used to store the integer codes
        -:175712:**                       that represent terminal and non-terminal symbols.
        -:175713:**                       "unsigned char" is used if there are fewer than
        -:175714:**                       256 symbols.  Larger types otherwise.
        -:175715:**    YYNOCODE           is a number of type YYCODETYPE that is not used for
        -:175716:**                       any terminal or nonterminal symbol.
        -:175717:**    YYFALLBACK         If defined, this indicates that one or more tokens
        -:175718:**                       (also known as: "terminal symbols") have fall-back
        -:175719:**                       values which should be used if the original symbol
        -:175720:**                       would not parse.  This permits keywords to sometimes
        -:175721:**                       be used as identifiers, for example.
        -:175722:**    YYACTIONTYPE       is the data type used for "action codes" - numbers
        -:175723:**                       that indicate what to do in response to the next
        -:175724:**                       token.
        -:175725:**    sqlite3ParserTOKENTYPE     is the data type used for minor type for terminal
        -:175726:**                       symbols.  Background: A "minor type" is a semantic
        -:175727:**                       value associated with a terminal or non-terminal
        -:175728:**                       symbols.  For example, for an "ID" terminal symbol,
        -:175729:**                       the minor type might be the name of the identifier.
        -:175730:**                       Each non-terminal can have a different minor type.
        -:175731:**                       Terminal symbols all have the same minor type, though.
        -:175732:**                       This macros defines the minor type for terminal
        -:175733:**                       symbols.
        -:175734:**    YYMINORTYPE        is the data type used for all minor types.
        -:175735:**                       This is typically a union of many types, one of
        -:175736:**                       which is sqlite3ParserTOKENTYPE.  The entry in the union
        -:175737:**                       for terminal symbols is called "yy0".
        -:175738:**    YYSTACKDEPTH       is the maximum depth of the parser's stack.  If
        -:175739:**                       zero the stack is dynamically sized using realloc()
        -:175740:**    sqlite3ParserARG_SDECL     A static variable declaration for the %extra_argument
        -:175741:**    sqlite3ParserARG_PDECL     A parameter declaration for the %extra_argument
        -:175742:**    sqlite3ParserARG_PARAM     Code to pass %extra_argument as a subroutine parameter
        -:175743:**    sqlite3ParserARG_STORE     Code to store %extra_argument into yypParser
        -:175744:**    sqlite3ParserARG_FETCH     Code to extract %extra_argument from yypParser
        -:175745:**    sqlite3ParserCTX_*         As sqlite3ParserARG_ except for %extra_context
        -:175746:**    YYREALLOC          Name of the realloc() function to use
        -:175747:**    YYFREE             Name of the free() function to use
        -:175748:**    YYDYNSTACK         True if stack space should be extended on heap
        -:175749:**    YYERRORSYMBOL      is the code number of the error symbol.  If not
        -:175750:**                       defined, then do no error processing.
        -:175751:**    YYNSTATE           the combined number of states.
        -:175752:**    YYNRULE            the number of rules in the grammar
        -:175753:**    YYNTOKEN           Number of terminal symbols
        -:175754:**    YY_MAX_SHIFT       Maximum value for shift actions
        -:175755:**    YY_MIN_SHIFTREDUCE Minimum value for shift-reduce actions
        -:175756:**    YY_MAX_SHIFTREDUCE Maximum value for shift-reduce actions
        -:175757:**    YY_ERROR_ACTION    The yy_action[] code for syntax error
        -:175758:**    YY_ACCEPT_ACTION   The yy_action[] code for accept
        -:175759:**    YY_NO_ACTION       The yy_action[] code for no-op
        -:175760:**    YY_MIN_REDUCE      Minimum value for reduce actions
        -:175761:**    YY_MAX_REDUCE      Maximum value for reduce actions
        -:175762:**    YY_MIN_DSTRCTR     Minimum symbol value that has a destructor
        -:175763:**    YY_MAX_DSTRCTR     Maximum symbol value that has a destructor
        -:175764:*/
        -:175765:#ifndef INTERFACE
        -:175766:# define INTERFACE 1
        -:175767:#endif
