        -:175859:/* Next are the tables used to determine what action to take based on the
        -:175860:** current state and lookahead token.  These tables are used to implement
        -:175861:** functions that take a state number and lookahead value and return an
        -:175862:** action integer.
        -:175863:**
        -:175864:** Suppose the action integer is N.  Then the action is determined as
        -:175865:** follows
        -:175866:**
        -:175867:**   0 <= N <= YY_MAX_SHIFT             Shift N.  That is, push the lookahead
        -:175868:**                                      token onto the stack and goto state N.
        -:175869:**
        -:175870:**   N between YY_MIN_SHIFTREDUCE       Shift to an arbitrary state then
        -:175871:**     and YY_MAX_SHIFTREDUCE           reduce by rule N-YY_MIN_SHIFTREDUCE.
        -:175872:**
        -:175873:**   N == YY_ERROR_ACTION               A syntax error has occurred.
        -:175874:**
        -:175875:**   N == YY_ACCEPT_ACTION              The parser accepts its input.
        -:175876:**
        -:175877:**   N == YY_NO_ACTION                  No such action.  Denotes unused
        -:175878:**                                      slots in the yy_action[] table.
        -:175879:**
        -:175880:**   N between YY_MIN_REDUCE            Reduce by rule N-YY_MIN_REDUCE
        -:175881:**     and YY_MAX_REDUCE
        -:175882:**
        -:175883:** The action table is constructed as a single large table named yy_action[].
        -:175884:** Given state S and lookahead X, the action is computed as either:
        -:175885:**
        -:175886:**    (A)   N = yy_action[ yy_shift_ofst[S] + X ]
        -:175887:**    (B)   N = yy_default[S]
        -:175888:**
        -:175889:** The (A) formula is preferred.  The B formula is used instead if
        -:175890:** yy_lookahead[yy_shift_ofst[S]+X] is not equal to X.
        -:175891:**
        -:175892:** The formulas above are for computing the action when the lookahead is
        -:175893:** a terminal symbol.  If the lookahead is a non-terminal (as occurs after
        -:175894:** a reduce action) then the yy_reduce_ofst[] array is used in place of
        -:175895:** the yy_shift_ofst[] array.
        -:175896:**
        -:175897:** The following are the tables generated in this section:
        -:175898:**
        -:175899:**  yy_action[]        A single table containing all actions.
        -:175900:**  yy_lookahead[]     A table containing the lookahead for each entry in
        -:175901:**                     yy_action.  Used to detect hash collisions.
        -:175902:**  yy_shift_ofst[]    For each state, the offset into yy_action for
        -:175903:**                     shifting terminals.
        -:175904:**  yy_reduce_ofst[]   For each state, the offset into yy_action for
        -:175905:**                     shifting non-terminals after a reduce.
        -:175906:**  yy_default[]       Default action for each state.
        -:175907:**
        -:175908:*********** Begin parsing tables **********************************************/
