        -:176549:/* The next table maps tokens (terminal symbols) into fallback tokens.
        -:176550:** If a construct like the following:
        -:176551:**
        -:176552:**      %fallback ID X Y Z.
        -:176553:**
        -:176554:** appears in the grammar, then ID becomes a fallback token for X, Y,
        -:176555:** and Z.  Whenever one of the tokens X, Y, or Z is input to the parser
        -:176556:** but it does not parse, the type of the token is changed to ID and
        -:176557:** the parse is retried before an error is thrown.
        -:176558:**
