        -:181566:/*
        -:181567:** The following three functions are called immediately after the tokenizer
        -:181568:** reads the keywords WINDOW, OVER and FILTER, respectively, to determine
        -:181569:** whether the token should be treated as a keyword or an SQL identifier.
        -:181570:** This cannot be handled by the usual lemon %fallback method, due to
        -:181571:** the ambiguity in some constructions. e.g.
        -:181572:**
        -:181573:**   SELECT sum(x) OVER ...
        -:181574:**
        -:181575:** In the above, "OVER" might be a keyword, or it might be an alias for the
        -:181576:** sum(x) expression. If a "%fallback ID OVER" directive were added to
        -:181577:** grammar, then SQLite would always treat "OVER" as an alias, making it
        -:181578:** impossible to call a window-function without a FILTER clause.
        -:181579:**
        -:181580:** WINDOW is treated as a keyword if:
        -:181581:**
        -:181582:**   * the following token is an identifier, or a keyword that can fallback
        -:181583:**     to being an identifier, and
        -:181584:**   * the token after than one is TK_AS.
        -:181585:**
        -:181586:** OVER is a keyword if:
