        -:188679:/*
        -:188680:** There are 2 different modes of operation for a hash table:
        -:188681:**
        -:188682:**   FTS3_HASH_STRING        pKey points to a string that is nKey bytes long
        -:188683:**                           (including the null-terminator, if any).  Case
        -:188684:**                           is respected in comparisons.
        -:188685:**
        -:188686:**   FTS3_HASH_BINARY        pKey points to binary data nKey bytes long.
        -:188687:**                           memcmp() is used to compare keys.
