        -:196881:** error) is returned and *ppExpr is set to 0.
        -:196882:**
        -:196883:** If parameter n is a negative number, then z is assumed to point to a
        -:196884:** nul-terminated string and the length is determined using strlen().
        -:196885:**
        -:196886:** The first parameter, pTokenizer, is passed the fts3 tokenizer module to
        -:196887:** use to normalize query tokens while parsing the expression. The azCol[]
        -:196888:** array, which is assumed to contain nCol entries, should contain the names
        -:196889:** of each column in the target fts3 table, in order from left to right.
