        -:198272:** to the sqlite3Fts3InitHashTable() function (e.g. 'fts3_tokenizer').
        -:198273:**
        -:198274:** If the <pointer> argument is specified, it must be a blob value
        -:198275:** containing a pointer to be stored as the hash data corresponding
        -:198276:** to the string <key-name>. If <pointer> is not specified, then
        -:198277:** the string <key-name> must already exist in the has table. Otherwise,
        -:198278:** an error is returned.
        -:198279:**
        -:198280:** Whether or not the <pointer> argument is specified, the value returned
        -:198281:** is a blob containing the pointer stored as the hash data corresponding
        -:198282:** to string <key-name> (after the hash-table is updated, if applicable).
        -:198283:*/
