        -:198987:******************************************************************************
        -:198988:**
        -:198989:** This file contains code for the "fts3tokenize" virtual table module.
        -:198990:** An fts3tokenize virtual table is created as follows:
        -:198991:**
        -:198992:**   CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE <tbl> USING fts3tokenize(
        -:198993:**       <tokenizer-name>, <arg-1>, ...
        -:198994:**   );
        -:198995:**
        -:198996:** The table created has the following schema:
        -:198997:**
        -:198998:**   CREATE TABLE <tbl>(input, token, start, end, position)
        -:198999:**
        -:199000:** When queried, the query must include a WHERE clause of type:
        -:199001:**
        -:199002:**   input = <string>
        -:199003:**
        -:199004:** The virtual table module tokenizes this <string>, using the FTS3
        -:199005:** tokenizer specified by the arguments to the CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE
        -:199006:** statement and returns one row for each token in the result. With
        -:199007:** fields set as follows:
        -:199008:**
        -:199009:**   input:   Always set to a copy of <string>
        -:199010:**   token:   A token from the input.
        -:199011:**   start:   Byte offset of the token within the input <string>.
        -:199012:**   end:     Byte offset of the byte immediately following the end of the
        -:199013:**            token within the input string.
        -:199014:**   pos:     Token offset of token within input.
