        -:213471:/*
        -:213472:** Database Format of R-Tree Tables
        -:213473:** --------------------------------
        -:213474:**
        -:213475:** The data structure for a single virtual r-tree table is stored in three
        -:213476:** native SQLite tables declared as follows. In each case, the '%' character
        -:213477:** in the table name is replaced with the user-supplied name of the r-tree
        -:213478:** table.
        -:213479:**
        -:213480:**   CREATE TABLE %_node(nodeno INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, data BLOB)
        -:213481:**   CREATE TABLE %_parent(nodeno INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, parentnode INTEGER)
        -:213482:**   CREATE TABLE %_rowid(rowid INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, nodeno INTEGER, ...)
        -:213483:**
        -:213484:** The data for each node of the r-tree structure is stored in the %_node
        -:213485:** table. For each node that is not the root node of the r-tree, there is
        -:213486:** an entry in the %_parent table associating the node with its parent.
        -:213487:** And for each row of data in the table, there is an entry in the %_rowid
        -:213488:** table that maps from the entries rowid to the id of the node that it
        -:213489:** is stored on.  If the r-tree contains auxiliary columns, those are stored
        -:213490:** on the end of the %_rowid table.
        -:213491:**
        -:213492:** The root node of an r-tree always exists, even if the r-tree table is
        -:213493:** empty. The nodeno of the root node is always 1. All other nodes in the
        -:213494:** table must be the same size as the root node. The content of each node
        -:213495:** is formatted as follows:
        -:213496:**
        -:213497:**   1. If the node is the root node (node 1), then the first 2 bytes
        -:213498:**      of the node contain the tree depth as a big-endian integer.
        -:213499:**      For non-root nodes, the first 2 bytes are left unused.
        -:213500:**
        -:213501:**   2. The next 2 bytes contain the number of entries currently
        -:213502:**      stored in the node.
        -:213503:**
        -:213504:**   3. The remainder of the node contains the node entries. Each entry
        -:213505:**      consists of a single 8-byte integer followed by an even number
        -:213506:**      of 4-byte coordinates. For leaf nodes the integer is the rowid
        -:213507:**      of a record. For internal nodes it is the node number of a
