        -:221236:/*
        -:221237:** Obtain an indication as to the current stage of an RBU update or vacuum.
        -:221238:** This function always returns one of the SQLITE_RBU_STATE_XXX constants
        -:221239:** defined in this file. Return values should be interpreted as follows:
        -:221240:**
        -:221241:** SQLITE_RBU_STATE_OAL:
        -:221242:**   RBU is currently building a *-oal file. The next call to sqlite3rbu_step()
        -:221243:**   may either add further data to the *-oal file, or compute data that will
        -:221244:**   be added by a subsequent call.
        -:221245:**
        -:221246:** SQLITE_RBU_STATE_MOVE:
        -:221247:**   RBU has finished building the *-oal file. The next call to sqlite3rbu_step()
        -:221248:**   will move the *-oal file to the equivalent *-wal path. If the current
        -:221249:**   operation is an RBU update, then the updated version of the database
        -:221250:**   file will become visible to ordinary SQLite clients following the next
        -:221251:**   call to sqlite3rbu_step().
        -:221252:**
        -:221253:** SQLITE_RBU_STATE_CHECKPOINT:
        -:221254:**   RBU is currently performing an incremental checkpoint. The next call to
        -:221255:**   sqlite3rbu_step() will copy a page of data from the *-wal file into
        -:221256:**   the target database file.
        -:221257:**
        -:221258:** SQLITE_RBU_STATE_DONE:
        -:221259:**   The RBU operation has finished. Any subsequent calls to sqlite3rbu_step()
        -:221260:**   will immediately return SQLITE_DONE.
        -:221261:**
        -:221262:** SQLITE_RBU_STATE_ERROR:
        -:221263:**   An error has occurred. Any subsequent calls to sqlite3rbu_step() will
        -:221264:**   immediately return the SQLite error code associated with the error.
        -:221265:*/
