        -:221272:SQLITE_API int sqlite3rbu_state(sqlite3rbu *pRbu);
        -:221273:
        -:221274:/*
        -:221275:** As part of applying an RBU update or performing an RBU vacuum operation,
        -:221276:** the system must at one point move the *-oal file to the equivalent *-wal
        -:221277:** path. Normally, it does this by invoking POSIX function rename(2) directly.
        -:221278:** Except on WINCE platforms, where it uses win32 API MoveFileW(). This
        -:221279:** function may be used to register a callback that the RBU module will invoke
        -:221280:** instead of one of these APIs.
        -:221281:**
        -:221282:** If a callback is registered with an RBU handle, it invokes it instead
        -:221283:** of rename(2) when it needs to move a file within the file-system. The
        -:221284:** first argument passed to the xRename() callback is a copy of the second
        -:221285:** argument (pArg) passed to this function. The second is the full path
        -:221286:** to the file to move and the third the full path to which it should be
        -:221287:** moved. The callback function should return SQLITE_OK to indicate
        -:221288:** success. If an error occurs, it should return an SQLite error code.
        -:221289:** In this case the RBU operation will be abandoned and the error returned
        -:221290:** to the RBU user.
        -:221291:**
        -:221292:** Passing a NULL pointer in place of the xRename argument to this function
        -:221293:** restores the default behaviour.
        -:221294:*/
        -:221295:SQLITE_API void sqlite3rbu_rename_handler(
        -:221296:  sqlite3rbu *pRbu,
        -:221297:  void *pArg,
        -:221298:  int (*xRename)(void *pArg, const char *zOld, const char *zNew)
        -:221299:);
        -:221300:
        -:221301:
        -:221302:/*
        -:221303:** Create an RBU VFS named zName that accesses the underlying file-system
        -:221304:** via existing VFS zParent. Or, if the zParent parameter is passed NULL,
        -:221305:** then the new RBU VFS uses the default system VFS to access the file-system.
        -:221306:** The new object is registered as a non-default VFS with SQLite before
        -:221307:** returning.
        -:221308:**
        -:221309:** Part of the RBU implementation uses a custom VFS object. Usually, this
        -:221310:** object is created and deleted automatically by RBU.
        -:221311:**
        -:221312:** The exception is for applications that also use zipvfs. In this case,
        -:221313:** the custom VFS must be explicitly created by the user before the RBU
        -:221314:** handle is opened. The RBU VFS should be installed so that the zipvfs
        -:221315:** VFS uses the RBU VFS, which in turn uses any other VFS layers in use
        -:221316:** (for example multiplexor) to access the file-system. For example,
        -:221317:** to assemble an RBU enabled VFS stack that uses both zipvfs and
        -:221318:** multiplexor (error checking omitted):
        -:221319:**
        -:221320:**     // Create a VFS named "multiplex" (not the default).
        -:221321:**     sqlite3_multiplex_initialize(0, 0);
        -:221322:**
        -:221323:**     // Create an rbu VFS named "rbu" that uses multiplexor. If the
        -:221324:**     // second argument were replaced with NULL, the "rbu" VFS would
        -:221325:**     // access the file-system via the system default VFS, bypassing the
        -:221326:**     // multiplexor.
        -:221327:**     sqlite3rbu_create_vfs("rbu", "multiplex");
        -:221328:**
        -:221329:**     // Create a zipvfs VFS named "zipvfs" that uses rbu.
        -:221330:**     zipvfs_create_vfs_v3("zipvfs", "rbu", 0, xCompressorAlgorithmDetector);
        -:221331:**
        -:221332:**     // Make zipvfs the default VFS.
        -:221333:**     sqlite3_vfs_register(sqlite3_vfs_find("zipvfs"), 1);
        -:221334:**
        -:221335:** Because the default VFS created above includes a RBU functionality, it
        -:221336:** may be used by RBU clients. Attempting to use RBU with a zipvfs VFS stack
        -:221337:** that does not include the RBU layer results in an error.
        -:221338:**
        -:221339:** The overhead of adding the "rbu" VFS to the system is negligible for
        -:221340:** non-RBU users. There is no harm in an application accessing the
        -:221341:** file-system via "rbu" all the time, even if it only uses RBU functionality
        -:221342:** occasionally.
        -:221343:*/
        -:221344:SQLITE_API int sqlite3rbu_create_vfs(const char *zName, const char *zParent);
        -:221345:
        -:221346:/*
        -:221347:** Deregister and destroy an RBU vfs created by an earlier call to
        -:221348:** sqlite3rbu_create_vfs().
        -:221349:**
        -:221350:** VFS objects are not reference counted. If a VFS object is destroyed
        -:221351:** before all database handles that use it have been closed, the results
        -:221352:** are undefined.
        -:221353:*/
        -:221354:SQLITE_API void sqlite3rbu_destroy_vfs(const char *zName);
