        -:225743:/**************************************************************************
        -:225744:** Beginning of RBU VFS shim methods. The VFS shim modifies the behaviour
        -:225745:** of a standard VFS in the following ways:
        -:225746:**
        -:225747:** 1. Whenever the first page of a main database file is read or
        -:225748:**    written, the value of the change-counter cookie is stored in
        -:225749:**    rbu_file.iCookie. Similarly, the value of the "write-version"
        -:225750:**    database header field is stored in rbu_file.iWriteVer. This ensures
        -:225751:**    that the values are always trustworthy within an open transaction.
        -:225752:**
        -:225753:** 2. Whenever an SQLITE_OPEN_WAL file is opened, the (rbu_file.pWalFd)
        -:225754:**    member variable of the associated database file descriptor is set
        -:225755:**    to point to the new file. A mutex protected linked list of all main
        -:225756:**    db fds opened using a particular RBU VFS is maintained at
        -:225757:**    rbu_vfs.pMain to facilitate this.
        -:225758:**
        -:225759:** 3. Using a new file-control "SQLITE_FCNTL_RBU", a main db rbu_file
        -:225760:**    object can be marked as the target database of an RBU update. This
        -:225761:**    turns on the following extra special behaviour:
        -:225762:**
        -:225763:** 3a. If xAccess() is called to check if there exists a *-wal file
        -:225764:**     associated with an RBU target database currently in RBU_STAGE_OAL
        -:225765:**     stage (preparing the *-oal file), the following special handling
        -:225766:**     applies:
        -:225767:**
        -:225768:**      * if the *-wal file does exist, return SQLITE_CANTOPEN. An RBU
        -:225769:**        target database may not be in wal mode already.
        -:225770:**
        -:225771:**      * if the *-wal file does not exist, set the output parameter to
        -:225772:**        non-zero (to tell SQLite that it does exist) anyway.
        -:225773:**
        -:225774:**     Then, when xOpen() is called to open the *-wal file associated with
        -:225775:**     the RBU target in RBU_STAGE_OAL stage, instead of opening the *-wal
        -:225776:**     file, the rbu vfs opens the corresponding *-oal file instead.
        -:225777:**
        -:225778:** 3b. The *-shm pages returned by xShmMap() for a target db file in
        -:225779:**     RBU_STAGE_OAL mode are actually stored in heap memory. This is to
        -:225780:**     avoid creating a *-shm file on disk. Additionally, xShmLock() calls
        -:225781:**     are no-ops on target database files in RBU_STAGE_OAL mode. This is
        -:225782:**     because assert() statements in some VFS implementations fail if
        -:225783:**     xShmLock() is called before xShmMap().
        -:225784:**
        -:225785:** 3c. If an EXCLUSIVE lock is attempted on a target database file in any
        -:225786:**     mode except RBU_STAGE_DONE (all work completed and checkpointed), it
        -:225787:**     fails with an SQLITE_BUSY error. This is to stop RBU connections
        -:225788:**     from automatically checkpointing a *-wal (or *-oal) file from within
        -:225789:**     sqlite3_close().
        -:225790:**
        -:225791:** 3d. In RBU_STAGE_CAPTURE mode, all xRead() calls on the wal file, and
        -:225792:**     all xWrite() calls on the target database file perform no IO.
        -:225793:**     Instead the frame and page numbers that would be read and written
        -:225794:**     are recorded. Additionally, successful attempts to obtain exclusive
        -:225795:**     xShmLock() WRITER, CHECKPOINTER and READ0 locks on the target
        -:225796:**     database file are recorded. xShmLock() calls to unlock the same
        -:225797:**     locks are no-ops (so that once obtained, these locks are never
        -:225798:**     relinquished). Finally, calls to xSync() on the target database
        -:225799:**     file fail with SQLITE_NOTICE errors.
        -:225800:*/
        -:225801:
        -:225802:static void rbuUnlockShm(rbu_file *p){
        -:225803:  assert( p->openFlags & SQLITE_OPEN_MAIN_DB );
        -:225804:  if( p->pRbu ){
        -:225805:    int (*xShmLock)(sqlite3_file*,int,int,int) = p->pReal->pMethods->xShmLock;
        -:225806:    int i;
        -:225807:    for(i=0; i<SQLITE_SHM_NLOCK;i++){
        -:225808:      if( (1<<i) & p->pRbu->mLock ){
        -:225809:        xShmLock(p->pReal, i, 1, SQLITE_SHM_UNLOCK|SQLITE_SHM_EXCLUSIVE);
        -:225810:      }
        -:225811:    }
        -:225812:    p->pRbu->mLock = 0;
        -:225813:  }
        -:225814:}
