        -:244264:**
        -:244265:******************************************************************************
        -:244266:**
        -:244267:** Low level access to the FTS index stored in the database file. The
        -:244268:** routines in this file file implement all read and write access to the
        -:244269:** %_data table. Other parts of the system access this functionality via
        -:244270:** the interface defined in fts5Int.h.
        -:244271:*/
        -:244272:
        -:244273:
        -:244274:/* #include "fts5Int.h" */
        -:244275:
        -:244276:/*
        -:244277:** Overview:
        -:244278:**
        -:244279:** The %_data table contains all the FTS indexes for an FTS5 virtual table.
        -:244280:** As well as the main term index, there may be up to 31 prefix indexes.
        -:244281:** The format is similar to FTS3/4, except that:
        -:244282:**
        -:244283:**   * all segment b-tree leaf data is stored in fixed size page records
        -:244284:**     (e.g. 1000 bytes). A single doclist may span multiple pages. Care is
        -:244285:**     taken to ensure it is possible to iterate in either direction through
        -:244286:**     the entries in a doclist, or to seek to a specific entry within a
        -:244287:**     doclist, without loading it into memory.
        -:244288:**
        -:244289:**   * large doclists that span many pages have associated "doclist index"
        -:244290:**     records that contain a copy of the first rowid on each page spanned by
        -:244291:**     the doclist. This is used to speed up seek operations, and merges of
        -:244292:**     large doclists with very small doclists.
        -:244293:**
        -:244294:**   * extra fields in the "structure record" record the state of ongoing
        -:244295:**     incremental merge operations.
        -:244296:**
        -:244297:*/
        -:244298:
        -:244299:
        -:244300:#define FTS5_OPT_WORK_UNIT  1000  /* Number of leaf pages per optimize step */
        -:244301:#define FTS5_WORK_UNIT      64    /* Number of leaf pages in unit of work */
        -:244302:
        -:244303:#define FTS5_MIN_DLIDX_SIZE 4     /* Add dlidx if this many empty pages */
        -:244304:
        -:244305:#define FTS5_MAIN_PREFIX '0'
        -:244306:
        -:244307:#if FTS5_MAX_PREFIX_INDEXES > 31
        -:244308:# error "FTS5_MAX_PREFIX_INDEXES is too large"
        -:244309:#endif
        -:244310:
        -:244311:#define FTS5_MAX_LEVEL 64
        -:244312:
        -:244313:/*
        -:244314:** There are two versions of the format used for the structure record:
        -:244315:**
        -:244316:**   1. the legacy format, that may be read by all fts5 versions, and
        -:244317:**
        -:244318:**   2. the V2 format, which is used by contentless_delete=1 databases.
        -:244319:**
        -:244320:** Both begin with a 4-byte "configuration cookie" value. Then, a legacy
        -:244321:** format structure record contains a varint - the number of levels in
        -:244322:** the structure. Whereas a V2 structure record contains the constant
        -:244323:** 4 bytes [0xff 0x00 0x00 0x01]. This is unambiguous as the value of a
        -:244324:** varint has to be at least 16256 to begin with "0xFF". And the default
        -:244325:** maximum number of levels is 64.
        -:244326:**
        -:244327:** See below for more on structure record formats.
        -:244328:*/
        -:244329:#define FTS5_STRUCTURE_V2 "\xFF\x00\x00\x01"
        -:244330:
        -:244331:/*
        -:244332:** Details:
        -:244333:**
        -:244334:** The %_data table managed by this module,
        -:244335:**
        -:244336:**     CREATE TABLE %_data(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, block BLOB);
        -:244337:**
        -:244338:** , contains the following 6 types of records. See the comments surrounding
        -:244339:** the FTS5_*_ROWID macros below for a description of how %_data rowids are
        -:244340:** assigned to each fo them.
        -:244341:**
        -:244342:** 1. Structure Records:
        -:244343:**
        -:244344:**   The set of segments that make up an index - the index structure - are
        -:244345:**   recorded in a single record within the %_data table. The record consists
        -:244346:**   of a single 32-bit configuration cookie value followed by a list of
        -:244347:**   SQLite varints.
        -:244348:**
        -:244349:**   If the structure record is a V2 record, the configuration cookie is
        -:244350:**   followed by the following 4 bytes: [0xFF 0x00 0x00 0x01].
        -:244351:**
        -:244352:**   Next, the record continues with three varints:
        -:244353:**
        -:244354:**     + number of levels,
        -:244355:**     + total number of segments on all levels,
        -:244356:**     + value of write counter.
        -:244357:**
        -:244358:**   Then, for each level from 0 to nMax:
        -:244359:**
        -:244360:**     + number of input segments in ongoing merge.
        -:244361:**     + total number of segments in level.
        -:244362:**     + for each segment from oldest to newest:
        -:244363:**         + segment id (always > 0)
        -:244364:**         + first leaf page number (often 1, always greater than 0)
        -:244365:**         + final leaf page number
        -:244366:**
        -:244367:**      Then, for V2 structures only:
        -:244368:**
        -:244369:**         + lower origin counter value,
        -:244370:**         + upper origin counter value,
        -:244371:**         + the number of tombstone hash pages.
        -:244372:**
        -:244373:** 2. The Averages Record:
        -:244374:**
        -:244375:**   A single record within the %_data table. The data is a list of varints.
        -:244376:**   The first value is the number of rows in the index. Then, for each column
        -:244377:**   from left to right, the total number of tokens in the column for all
        -:244378:**   rows of the table.
        -:244379:**
        -:244380:** 3. Segment leaves:
        -:244381:**
        -:244382:**   TERM/DOCLIST FORMAT:
        -:244383:**
        -:244384:**     Most of each segment leaf is taken up by term/doclist data. The
        -:244385:**     general format of term/doclist, starting with the first term
        -:244386:**     on the leaf page, is:
        -:244387:**
        -:244388:**         varint : size of first term
        -:244389:**         blob:    first term data
        -:244390:**         doclist: first doclist
        -:244391:**         zero-or-more {
        -:244392:**           varint:  number of bytes in common with previous term
        -:244393:**           varint:  number of bytes of new term data (nNew)
        -:244394:**           blob:    nNew bytes of new term data
        -:244395:**           doclist: next doclist
        -:244396:**         }
        -:244397:**
        -:244398:**     doclist format:
        -:244399:**
        -:244400:**         varint:  first rowid
        -:244401:**         poslist: first poslist
        -:244402:**         zero-or-more {
        -:244403:**           varint:  rowid delta (always > 0)
        -:244404:**           poslist: next poslist
        -:244405:**         }
        -:244406:**
        -:244407:**     poslist format:
        -:244408:**
        -:244409:**         varint: size of poslist in bytes multiplied by 2, not including
        -:244410:**                 this field. Plus 1 if this entry carries the "delete" flag.
        -:244411:**         collist: collist for column 0
        -:244412:**         zero-or-more {
        -:244413:**           0x01 byte
        -:244414:**           varint: column number (I)
        -:244415:**           collist: collist for column I
        -:244416:**         }
        -:244417:**
        -:244418:**     collist format:
        -:244419:**
        -:244420:**         varint: first offset + 2
        -:244421:**         zero-or-more {
        -:244422:**           varint: offset delta + 2
        -:244423:**         }
        -:244424:**
        -:244425:**   PAGE FORMAT
        -:244426:**
        -:244427:**     Each leaf page begins with a 4-byte header containing 2 16-bit
        -:244428:**     unsigned integer fields in big-endian format. They are:
        -:244429:**
        -:244430:**       * The byte offset of the first rowid on the page, if it exists
        -:244431:**         and occurs before the first term (otherwise 0).
        -:244432:**
        -:244433:**       * The byte offset of the start of the page footer. If the page
        -:244434:**         footer is 0 bytes in size, then this field is the same as the
        -:244435:**         size of the leaf page in bytes.
        -:244436:**
        -:244437:**     The page footer consists of a single varint for each term located
        -:244438:**     on the page. Each varint is the byte offset of the current term
        -:244439:**     within the page, delta-compressed against the previous value. In
        -:244440:**     other words, the first varint in the footer is the byte offset of
        -:244441:**     the first term, the second is the byte offset of the second less that
        -:244442:**     of the first, and so on.
        -:244443:**
        -:244444:**     The term/doclist format described above is accurate if the entire
        -:244445:**     term/doclist data fits on a single leaf page. If this is not the case,
        -:244446:**     the format is changed in two ways:
        -:244447:**
        -:244448:**       + if the first rowid on a page occurs before the first term, it
        -:244449:**         is stored as a literal value:
        -:244450:**
        -:244451:**             varint:  first rowid
        -:244452:**
        -:244453:**       + the first term on each page is stored in the same way as the
        -:244454:**         very first term of the segment:
        -:244455:**
        -:244456:**             varint : size of first term
        -:244457:**             blob:    first term data
        -:244458:**
        -:244459:** 5. Segment doclist indexes:
        -:244460:**
        -:244461:**   Doclist indexes are themselves b-trees, however they usually consist of
        -:244462:**   a single leaf record only. The format of each doclist index leaf page
        -:244463:**   is:
        -:244464:**
        -:244465:**     * Flags byte. Bits are:
        -:244466:**         0x01: Clear if leaf is also the root page, otherwise set.
        -:244467:**
        -:244468:**     * Page number of fts index leaf page. As a varint.
        -:244469:**
        -:244470:**     * First rowid on page indicated by previous field. As a varint.
        -:244471:**
        -:244472:**     * A list of varints, one for each subsequent termless page. A
        -:244473:**       positive delta if the termless page contains at least one rowid,
        -:244474:**       or an 0x00 byte otherwise.
        -:244475:**
        -:244476:**   Internal doclist index nodes are:
        -:244477:**
        -:244478:**     * Flags byte. Bits are:
        -:244479:**         0x01: Clear for root page, otherwise set.
        -:244480:**
        -:244481:**     * Page number of first child page. As a varint.
        -:244482:**
        -:244483:**     * Copy of first rowid on page indicated by previous field. As a varint.
        -:244484:**
        -:244485:**     * A list of delta-encoded varints - the first rowid on each subsequent
        -:244486:**       child page.
        -:244487:**
        -:244488:** 6. Tombstone Hash Page
        -:244489:**
        -:244490:**   These records are only ever present in contentless_delete=1 tables.
        -:244491:**   There are zero or more of these associated with each segment. They
        -:244492:**   are used to store the tombstone rowids for rows contained in the
        -:244493:**   associated segments.
        -:244494:**
        -:244495:**   The set of nHashPg tombstone hash pages associated with a single
        -:244496:**   segment together form a single hash table containing tombstone rowids.
        -:244497:**   To find the page of the hash on which a key might be stored:
        -:244498:**
        -:244499:**       iPg = (rowid % nHashPg)
        -:244500:**
        -:244501:**   Then, within page iPg, which has nSlot slots:
        -:244502:**
        -:244503:**       iSlot = (rowid / nHashPg) % nSlot
        -:244504:**
        -:244505:**   Each tombstone hash page begins with an 8 byte header:
        -:244506:**
        -:244507:**     1-byte:  Key-size (the size in bytes of each slot). Either 4 or 8.
        -:244508:**     1-byte:  rowid-0-tombstone flag. This flag is only valid on the
        -:244509:**              first tombstone hash page for each segment (iPg=0). If set,
        -:244510:**              the hash table contains rowid 0. If clear, it does not.
        -:244511:**              Rowid 0 is handled specially.
        -:244512:**     2-bytes: unused.
        -:244513:**     4-bytes: Big-endian integer containing number of entries on page.
        -:244514:**
        -:244515:**   Following this are nSlot 4 or 8 byte slots (depending on the key-size
        -:244516:**   in the first byte of the page header). The number of slots may be
        -:244517:**   determined based on the size of the page record and the key-size:
        -:244518:**
        -:244519:**     nSlot = (nByte - 8) / key-size
        -:244520:*/
        -:244521:
        -:244522:/*
        -:244523:** Rowids for the averages and structure records in the %_data table.
        -:244524:*/
        -:244525:#define FTS5_AVERAGES_ROWID     1    /* Rowid used for the averages record */
        -:244526:#define FTS5_STRUCTURE_ROWID   10    /* The structure record */
        -:244527:
        -:244528:/*
        -:244529:** Macros determining the rowids used by segment leaves and dlidx leaves
        -:244530:** and nodes. All nodes and leaves are stored in the %_data table with large
        -:244531:** positive rowids.
        -:244532:**
        -:244533:** Each segment has a unique non-zero 16-bit id.
        -:244534:**
        -:244535:** The rowid for each segment leaf is found by passing the segment id and
        -:244536:** the leaf page number to the FTS5_SEGMENT_ROWID macro. Leaves are numbered
        -:244537:** sequentially starting from 1.
        -:244538:*/
        -:244539:#define FTS5_DATA_ID_B     16     /* Max seg id number 65535 */
        -:244540:#define FTS5_DATA_DLI_B     1     /* Doclist-index flag (1 bit) */
        -:244541:#define FTS5_DATA_HEIGHT_B  5     /* Max dlidx tree height of 32 */
        -:244542:#define FTS5_DATA_PAGE_B   31     /* Max page number of 2147483648 */
        -:244543:
        -:244544:#define fts5_dri(segid, dlidx, height, pgno) (                                 \
        -:244545: ((i64)(segid)  << (FTS5_DATA_PAGE_B+FTS5_DATA_HEIGHT_B+FTS5_DATA_DLI_B)) +    \
        -:244546: ((i64)(dlidx)  << (FTS5_DATA_PAGE_B + FTS5_DATA_HEIGHT_B)) +                  \
        -:244547: ((i64)(height) << (FTS5_DATA_PAGE_B)) +                                       \
        -:244548: ((i64)(pgno))                                                                 \
        -:244549:)
        -:244550:
        -:244551:#define FTS5_SEGMENT_ROWID(segid, pgno)       fts5_dri(segid, 0, 0, pgno)
        -:244552:#define FTS5_DLIDX_ROWID(segid, height, pgno) fts5_dri(segid, 1, height, pgno)
        -:244553:#define FTS5_TOMBSTONE_ROWID(segid,ipg)       fts5_dri(segid+(1<<16), 0, 0, ipg)
        -:244554:
        -:244555:#ifdef SQLITE_DEBUG
        -:244556:static int sqlite3Fts5Corrupt() { return SQLITE_CORRUPT_VTAB; }
        -:244557:#endif
        -:244558:
        -:244559:
        -:244560:/*
        -:244561:** Each time a blob is read from the %_data table, it is padded with this
        -:244562:** many zero bytes. This makes it easier to decode the various record formats
        -:244563:** without overreading if the records are corrupt.
        -:244564:*/
        -:244565:#define FTS5_DATA_ZERO_PADDING 8
        -:244566:#define FTS5_DATA_PADDING 20
        -:244567:
        -:244568:typedef struct Fts5Data Fts5Data;
        -:244569:typedef struct Fts5DlidxIter Fts5DlidxIter;
        -:244570:typedef struct Fts5DlidxLvl Fts5DlidxLvl;
        -:244571:typedef struct Fts5DlidxWriter Fts5DlidxWriter;
        -:244572:typedef struct Fts5Iter Fts5Iter;
