        -:253775:**     xRollback(): Rollback the transaction.
        -:253776:**
        -:253777:** Anything that is required as part of a commit that may fail is performed
        -:253778:** in the xSync() callback. Current versions of SQLite ignore any errors
        -:253779:** returned by xCommit().
        -:253780:**
        -:253781:** And as sub-transactions are opened/closed:
        -:253782:**
        -:253783:**     xSavepoint(int S):  Open savepoint S.
        -:253784:**     xRelease(int S):    Commit and close savepoint S.
        -:253785:**     xRollbackTo(int S): Rollback to start of savepoint S.
        -:253786:**
        -:253787:** During a write-transaction the fts5_index.c module may cache some data
        -:253788:** in-memory. It is flushed to disk whenever xSync(), xRelease() or
        -:253789:** xSavepoint() is called. And discarded whenever xRollback() or xRollbackTo()
        -:253790:** is called.
