        -:254260:/*
        -:254261:** Implementation of the xBestIndex method for FTS5 tables. Within the
        -:254262:** WHERE constraint, it searches for the following:
        -:254263:**
        -:254264:**   1. A MATCH constraint against the table column.
        -:254265:**   2. A MATCH constraint against the "rank" column.
        -:254266:**   3. A MATCH constraint against some other column.
        -:254267:**   4. An == constraint against the rowid column.
        -:254268:**   5. A < or <= constraint against the rowid column.
        -:254269:**   6. A > or >= constraint against the rowid column.
        -:254270:**
        -:254271:** Within the ORDER BY, the following are supported:
        -:254272:**
        -:254273:**   5. ORDER BY rank [ASC|DESC]
        -:254274:**   6. ORDER BY rowid [ASC|DESC]
        -:254275:**
        -:254276:** Information for the xFilter call is passed via both the idxNum and
        -:254277:** idxStr variables. Specifically, idxNum is a bitmask of the following
        -:254278:** flags used to encode the ORDER BY clause:
        -:254279:**
        -:254280:**     FTS5_BI_ORDER_RANK
        -:254281:**     FTS5_BI_ORDER_ROWID
        -:254282:**     FTS5_BI_ORDER_DESC
        -:254283:**
        -:254284:** idxStr is used to encode data from the WHERE clause. For each argument
        -:254285:** passed to the xFilter method, the following is appended to idxStr:
        -:254286:**
        -:254287:**   Match against table column:            "m"
        -:254288:**   Match against rank column:             "r"
        -:254289:**   Match against other column:            "M<column-number>"
        -:254290:**   LIKE  against other column:            "L<column-number>"
        -:254291:**   GLOB  against other column:            "G<column-number>"
        -:254292:**   Equality constraint against the rowid: "="
        -:254293:**   A < or <= against the rowid:           "<"
        -:254294:**   A > or >= against the rowid:           ">"
        -:254295:**
        -:254296:** This function ensures that there is at most one "r" or "=". And that if
        -:254297:** there exists an "=" then there is no "<" or ">".
        -:254298:**
        -:254299:** If an unusable MATCH operator is present in the WHERE clause, then
        -:254300:** SQLITE_CONSTRAINT is returned.
        -:254301:**
